<PARA INFOID = "T010258A123" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "8Dec2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Spark Plug</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>High-ignitability iridium spark plugs have been adopted.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A thin needle-shaped iridium alloy is used for the center electrode and a thin needle-shaped platinum alloy for the ground electrode. Because iridium alloy has extremely high wear resistance, the center electrode can be made thinner, enabling more reliable ignition.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By adopting a long-reach type<HINTREF REFID = "H478010258A12301"/>, ignition performance has been improved and the cylinder head coolant passages around the spark plugs have been optimized.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<HINT>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT ID = "H478010258A12301">Conventional spark plugs can also be installed, but they are not interchangeable. In addition, if long-reach plugs are installed in an engine that uses conventional spark plugs, they may interfere with the pistons, so always install the specified spark plugs when replacing the plugs.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></HINT>
